IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `hca-dates`

-- Health Complaints Act 1995 (Tas) -- the rules a person who complains about a health service meets: what is a "health
-- service" (s 3, Schedule 1), who may complain (ss 22, 22A), what may be complained of (s 23(1)), the form of a
-- complaint (s 23(3)-(5)), the 2-year time limit and the other grounds on which a complaint must be dismissed (s 25(5),
-- (6)), dismissal for not meeting a requirement for information (ss 24, 25(7)), the time for assessment and for notice
-- of it (ss 25(1), (1C), (1CA), 27), withdrawal (s 30), conciliation (ss 25(4), 32A, 33, 37, 39), the investigation
-- report and the statement of decision on a prohibition order (ss 55(2), 56AAD(2)), the provider's answer to a notice of
-- recommended action (s 56), protection of the complainant's identity (s 64), intimidation and reprisals (ss 67, 68),
-- the time for prosecuting them (s 71) and protection from civil actions (s 73).
--
-- This module holds the law. The questions are asked in hca-seat.l4, which IMPORTs it and never restates a rule.
-- Nothing here is exported.
--
-- ANSWERS. A yes/no rule answers JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE where the Act's own words say no ("means", "must not", "is not
-- binding unless", "may not ... except where", an "if" or "where" condition that fails, a period the Act fixes); or
-- NOTHING where the Act does not answer on the facts given, with a "NOTHING-kind" comment. Judgments the Act leaves to
-- the Commissioner or a court ("satisfied", "of the opinion", "considers", "believes on reasonable grounds", "good
-- faith", "reasonable excuse") are inputs: the answer is conditional on them, never a guess at them.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on material from the Tasmanian Legislation website at 6 November 2026 (c) State of Tasmania, CC BY
-- 4.0; not the authorised version. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Health Complaints Act 1995`

GIVEN `the answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is yes` `the answer` IF
    CONSIDER `the answer`
    WHEN JUST b THEN b
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `s 3, Schedule 1 -- health service`

-- s 3: "health service means -- (a) a service provided to a person for, or purportedly for, the benefit of human health
-- -- (i) including services specified in Part 1 of Schedule 1; but (ii) excluding services specified in Part 2 of
-- Schedule 1; or (b) an administrative service directly related to a health service specified in paragraph (a) -- but
-- does not include a service that is prescribed by the regulations as not being a health service". The regulations are
-- not deposited: whether a service is prescribed is asked as a fact.
DECLARE `Kind of service` IS ONE OF
    `a service at a hospital, health institution or nursing home`
    `a medical, dental, pharmaceutical, mental health, community health, environmental health or specialized health service`
    `care, treatment or accommodation of aged persons or persons with a physical disability or mental dysfunction`
    `a laboratory service in support of a health service`
    `a laundry, dry cleaning, catering or other support service that affects a patient's or resident's care or treatment`
    `a social work, welfare, recreational or leisure service provided as part of a health service`
    `an ambulance service`
    `another service for, or purportedly for, the care or treatment of another person`
    `an allied health, therapeutic or technical service for the care or treatment of another person`
    `massage, naturopathy, acupuncture or another natural or alternative health care or diagnostic service`
    `information on the promotion or provision of health care, or health education`
    `temporary storage of human remains at a hospital or health institution`
    `another service by a person registered by a registration board`
    `another service for, or purportedly for, the benefit of human health`
    `an administrative service directly related to a health service`
    `an opinion or decision for a claim under the Workers Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 1988`
    `an opinion or decision for an application under the Asbestos-Related Diseases (Occupational Exposure) Compensation Act 2011`
    `a service not for the benefit of human health`

-- A "means" definition with an exclusion list (Part 2) and an exclusion by regulation ("does not include"): JUST FALSE
-- for those, and for a service that is not for the benefit of human health.
GIVEN `the service` IS A `Kind of service`
      `the regulations prescribe it as not a health service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3 -- it is a health service` `the service` `the regulations prescribe it as not a health service` MEANS
    IF `the regulations prescribe it as not a health service`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE CONSIDER `the service`
         WHEN `an opinion or decision for a claim under the Workers Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 1988` THEN JUST FALSE
         WHEN `an opinion or decision for an application under the Asbestos-Related Diseases (Occupational Exposure) Compensation Act 2011` THEN JUST FALSE
         WHEN `a service not for the benefit of human health` THEN JUST FALSE
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `ss 22, 22A -- who may complain`

-- s 22: "Any of the following persons is entitled to make a complaint to the Commissioner about a health service
-- sought, used or received by, or administered to, a health service user: (a) the health service user; (b) in the case
-- of a health service user who is a child -- (i) where the child has attained the age of 14 years, a person appointed
-- by that child ...; or (ii) where the child has not attained the age of 14 years, a parent or guardian of that child;
-- or (iii) where the Commissioner is of the opinion that the child is capable ..., the child; (d) the donee of a power
-- of attorney ... whose authority includes the making of a complaint under this Act; (e) where a person, under any
-- other law or an order of a court, has the care of the affairs of the health service user, that person; (f) where it
-- is difficult or impossible for the health service user to make a complaint ..., a person approved by the
-- Commissioner; (g) a health service provider; (h) the Minister; (i) the Health Minister; (j) the Secretary of the
-- Health Department; (k) if the Commissioner considers that ... a person other than a person referred to in paragraph
-- (a) to (j) (inclusive) should be permitted to make a complaint, that person." s 3: "child means a person who has not
-- attained the age of 18 years".
-- s 22A: "Any person may make a complaint to the Commissioner that a health care worker has acted in a manner that is in
-- breach of a code of conduct."
DECLARE `Who I am` IS ONE OF
    `the health service user`
    `a person the child appointed to complain for them`
    `a parent or guardian of the child`
    `the donee of a power of attorney from the health service user`
    `a person who has the care of the user's affairs under a law or a court order`
    `a person the Commissioner approved because the user cannot complain`
    `a health service provider`
    `the Minister, the Health Minister or the Secretary of the Health Department`
    `someone else`

-- (k) closes the list: anyone not in (a)-(j) is entitled only if the Commissioner considers that he or she should be
-- permitted, and s 25(5)(a) makes the Commissioner dismiss a complaint by a person not entitled. So a person outside
-- (a)-(j) whom the Commissioner has not permitted gets JUST FALSE (fork F2). Each paragraph's "where" or "in the case
-- of" condition that fails sends the person to (k).
GIVEN `who I am` IS A `Who I am`
      `the user's age in whole years` IS A NUMBER
      `the power of attorney covers complaints under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is difficult or impossible for the user to complain` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner has approved me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner considers I should be permitted to complain` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the complaint is that a health care worker breached a code of conduct` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 22, 22A -- I am entitled to complain` `who I am` `the user's age in whole years` `the power of attorney covers complaints under this Act` `it is difficult or impossible for the user to complain` `the Commissioner has approved me` `the Commissioner considers I should be permitted to complain` `the complaint is that a health care worker breached a code of conduct` MEANS
    IF `the complaint is that a health care worker breached a code of conduct`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `the paragraph (a) to (j) applies`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE IF `the Commissioner considers I should be permitted to complain`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `the user is a child` MEANS `the user's age in whole years` LESS THAN 18
        `the paragraph (a) to (j) applies` MEANS
            CONSIDER `who I am`
            WHEN `the health service user` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a person the child appointed to complain for them` THEN
                `the user is a child` AND `the user's age in whole years` AT LEAST 14
            WHEN `a parent or guardian of the child` THEN
                `the user's age in whole years` LESS THAN 14
            WHEN `the donee of a power of attorney from the health service user` THEN
                `the power of attorney covers complaints under this Act`
            WHEN `a person who has the care of the user's affairs under a law or a court order` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a person the Commissioner approved because the user cannot complain` THEN
                `it is difficult or impossible for the user to complain` AND `the Commissioner has approved me`
            WHEN `a health service provider` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `the Minister, the Health Minister or the Secretary of the Health Department` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `ss 23(1), 25(5)(b) -- what may be complained of`

-- s 23(1): "A person who is entitled to make a complaint under section 22 may make one or more of the following
-- complaints". s 25(5)(b): the Commissioner must dismiss a complaint if satisfied that "the complaint does not disclose a
-- subject matter of complaint referred to in section 23".
DECLARE `Ground of complaint` IS ONE OF
    `the provider acted unreasonably by not providing a health service`
    `the health service or part of it was not necessary`
    `the provider acted unreasonably in the manner of providing a health service`
    `the provider failed to exercise due skill`
    `the provider failed to treat the user in an appropriate professional manner`
    `the provider failed to respect the user's privacy or dignity`
    `the user was not given the information, choice, advice or prognosis section 23(1)(g) describes`
    `the provider unreasonably denied or restricted access to the user's records, or withheld information about the user's condition`
    `the provider acted unreasonably in disclosing information about the user`
    `the provider did not take proper action on the user's complaint to it`
    `the provider acted in another way inconsistent with the Charter`
    `a health care worker breached a code of conduct, and nothing else`
    `something else`

-- s 23(1) names its grounds and s 25(5)(b) dismisses a complaint that discloses none of them: JUST FALSE for something
-- else. A complaint under s 22A only (a code-of-conduct breach that is not also a s 23 ground) is not a "subject matter
-- of complaint referred to in section 23", read literally; s 22A entitles any person to make it. The Act does not
-- reconcile the two (finding 2): NOTHING-kind: the text conflicts (fork F3).
GIVEN `the ground` IS A `Ground of complaint`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 23(1), 25(5)(b) -- the complaint discloses a ground` `the ground` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `something else` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `a health care worker breached a code of conduct, and nothing else` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 23(3)-(5) -- the form of a complaint`

-- s 23(3): "Subject to this section, a complaint -- (a) is to be in writing; and (b) is to be signed by the complainant;
-- and (c) is to disclose the name and address of the complainant." (4): "The Commissioner may accept a complaint that
-- does not comply with subsection (3)." (5): an oral complaint accepted is to be put in writing and signed, unless the
-- Commissioner is satisfied there are good reasons for not doing so.
DECLARE `Form of my complaint` IS ONE OF
    `in the form section 23(3) asks for`
    `not in that form, and the Commissioner may still accept it`
    `accepted orally, and you must put it in writing and sign it if the Commissioner requires`

GIVEN `in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `signed by me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `gives my name and address` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner has accepted it orally` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Form of my complaint`
`s 23(3)-(5) -- the form of my complaint` `in writing` `signed by me` `gives my name and address` `the Commissioner has accepted it orally` MEANS
    IF `in writing` AND `signed by me` AND `gives my name and address`
    THEN `in the form section 23(3) asks for`
    ELSE IF (NOT `in writing`) AND `the Commissioner has accepted it orally`
         THEN `accepted orally, and you must put it in writing and sign it if the Commissioner requires`
         ELSE `not in that form, and the Commissioner may still accept it`

§§ `s 25(5)(c), (ca), (6) -- the 2-year time limit`

-- s 25(5): the Commissioner must dismiss a complaint if satisfied that "(c) the health service user became aware of the
-- circumstances that gave rise to the complaint more than 2 years before the complaint was made; or (ca) in the case of
-- a complaint relating to a health care worker, the complainant became aware of the circumstances ... more than 2 years
-- before the complaint was made". (6): "Subsection (5)(c) and (ca) do not apply where the Commissioner is satisfied that
-- the complainant had good reason for not making the complaint within 2 years of becoming aware of the circumstances".
--
-- Awareness on day A is not "more than 2 years before" a complaint made on or before the corresponding day 2 years after
-- A, so that corresponding day is the last day (fork F1). For a complaint relating to a health care
-- worker both clocks run, (c) on the user's awareness and (ca) on the complainant's: the earlier last day governs
-- (finding 3).
GIVEN `the day the user became aware` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 25(5)(c) -- the last day for complaining` `the day the user became aware` MEANS
    `the corresponding day` 24 `months after` `the day the user became aware`

GIVEN `the day the user became aware` IS A DATE
      `it relates to a health care worker` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I became aware` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 25(5)(c), (ca) -- the last day for my complaint` `the day the user became aware` `it relates to a health care worker` `the day I became aware` MEANS
    IF `it relates to a health care worker`
    THEN `the earlier of` (`s 25(5)(c) -- the last day for complaining` `the day the user became aware`) `and` (`s 25(5)(c) -- the last day for complaining` `the day I became aware`)
    ELSE `s 25(5)(c) -- the last day for complaining` `the day the user became aware`

-- The regulative rule: the complainant must make the complaint within the 2 years, lest the Commissioner must dismiss
-- it. The rule starts on the day of awareness (time 0); a step on day n is at time n. Never exported.
DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    `the complainant`
    `the parties to the conciliation`
    `the health service provider`

DECLARE `Step` IS ONE OF
    `make the complaint`
    `satisfy the Commissioner's requirement`
    `put the agreement in writing`
    `advise the Commissioner of the action taken`

GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
`s 25(5)(c) -- complain within 2 years` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the complainant`
    MUST `make the complaint`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the complainant` BECAUSE "the complaint was made more than 2 years after the circumstances became known, and the Commissioner must dismiss it unless satisfied there was good reason for the delay (s 25(5)(c), (ca), (6))"

-- JUST TRUE when the complaint is in time, or (s 25(6)) the Commissioner is satisfied of a good reason; JUST FALSE when
-- the period the Act fixes has passed and there is no such reason.
GIVEN `the day the user became aware` IS A DATE
      `it relates to a health care worker` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I became aware` IS A DATE
      `the day I complain` IS A DATE
      `the Commissioner is satisfied I had good reason for the delay` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25(5)(c), (ca), (6) -- my complaint is in time` `the day the user became aware` `it relates to a health care worker` `the day I became aware` `the day I complain` `the Commissioner is satisfied I had good reason for the delay` MEANS
    IF `the Commissioner is satisfied I had good reason for the delay`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`s 25(5)(c) -- complain within 2 years` `the days allowed`) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the complainant` `make the complaint` `the time of the complaint`))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN JUST TRUE
         OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `the first awareness` MEANS
            IF `it relates to a health care worker`
            THEN `the earlier of` `the day the user became aware` `and` `the day I became aware`
            ELSE `the day the user became aware`
        `the days allowed` MEANS `the days from` `the first awareness` `to` (`s 25(5)(c), (ca) -- the last day for my complaint` `the day the user became aware` `it relates to a health care worker` `the day I became aware`)
        `the time of the complaint` MEANS max 0 (`the days from` `the first awareness` `to` `the day I complain`)

§§ `s 25(5)(d)-(j) -- the other grounds on which a complaint must be dismissed`

-- s 25(5): "The Commissioner must dismiss a complaint if satisfied that -- ... (d) the complainant has failed, without
-- good reason, to take reasonable steps to resolve with the health service provider the grievance ...; (e) all the
-- issues ... have been adjudicated upon by a court, tribunal, board or other person ...; (f) a court has commenced to
-- hear a proceeding that relates to the subject matter of the complaint; (g) the complainant has been given reasonable
-- explanations and information and there would be no benefit in further entertaining the complaint; (h) the complaint
-- lacks substance; (i) the complaint is frivolous, vexatious or was not made in good faith; (j) the complaint has been
-- resolved." Each is the Commissioner's satisfaction, asked as a fact. An "if" condition: JUST FALSE when none holds
-- (s 25(5) does not then require dismissal; s 25(1A)(b)(iii) still lets the Commissioner dismiss).
GIVEN `no reasonable steps to resolve it with the provider, without good reason` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all the issues have been adjudicated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a court has commenced to hear a proceeding on the subject matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reasonable explanations given and no benefit in going on` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it lacks substance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is frivolous, vexatious or not in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has been resolved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25(5)(d)-(j) -- the Commissioner must dismiss it` `no reasonable steps to resolve it with the provider, without good reason` `all the issues have been adjudicated` `a court has commenced to hear a proceeding on the subject matter` `reasonable explanations given and no benefit in going on` `it lacks substance` `it is frivolous, vexatious or not in good faith` `it has been resolved` MEANS
    IF     `no reasonable steps to resolve it with the provider, without good reason`
        OR `all the issues have been adjudicated`
        OR `a court has commenced to hear a proceeding on the subject matter`
        OR `reasonable explanations given and no benefit in going on`
        OR `it lacks substance`
        OR `it is frivolous, vexatious or not in good faith`
        OR `it has been resolved`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 24, 25(7) -- a requirement for further information`

-- s 24(1): the Commissioner may require a complainant to provide further information or documents, or to verify the
-- complaint by statutory declaration, within a reasonable period the Commissioner specifies (s 24(2)) and may extend
-- (s 24(3)). s 25(7): "the Commissioner may dismiss the complaint if -- (a) the period for satisfying the requirement
-- has expired; and (b) after the expiration of that period, the Commissioner notified the complainant in writing that
-- the complaint might be dismissed unless the requirement was satisfied within 14 days after the notice was provided;
-- and (c) that period of 14 days has expired; and (d) the requirement is unsatisfied."
--
-- The regulative rule: from the day the warning notice is provided (time 0) the complainant must satisfy the
-- requirement within 14 days; the last day is the 14th day after. The 14 days are stated once, here, and both the rule
-- and the last day take them from this definition.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 25(7) -- the days after the warning` MEANS 14

GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
`s 25(7) -- satisfy the requirement within 14 days of the warning` MEANS
    PARTY `the complainant`
    MUST `satisfy the Commissioner's requirement`
    WITHIN `s 25(7) -- the days after the warning`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the complainant` BECAUSE "the requirement was not satisfied within 14 days after the Commissioner's written warning, so the Commissioner may dismiss the complaint (s 25(7))"

GIVEN `the day the warning was provided` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 25(7) -- the last day after the warning` `the day the warning was provided` MEANS `the day` `s 25(7) -- the days after the warning` `days after` `the day the warning was provided`

-- All four "if" conditions, on the day asked about: JUST TRUE (the Commissioner may dismiss) or JUST FALSE (s 25(7) does
-- not allow it on that day). A requirement satisfied late, but before the day asked about, fails (d).
GIVEN `the last day of the period set for the requirement` IS A DATE
      `a warning was provided` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the warning was provided` IS A DATE
      `I have satisfied the requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I satisfied it` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25(7) -- the Commissioner may dismiss my complaint on that day` `the last day of the period set for the requirement` `a warning was provided` `the day the warning was provided` `I have satisfied the requirement` `the day I satisfied it` `the day asked about` MEANS
    IF     `a warning was provided`
       AND `the days from` `the last day of the period set for the requirement` `to` `the day the warning was provided` GREATER THAN 0
       AND `the days from` `the last day of the period set for the requirement` `to` `the day asked about` GREATER THAN 0
       AND `the days from` (`s 25(7) -- the last day after the warning` `the day the warning was provided`) `to` `the day asked about` GREATER THAN 0
       AND (NOT `satisfied in the 14 days`)
       AND (NOT `satisfied by the day asked about`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `satisfied by the day asked about` MEANS
            `I have satisfied the requirement`
            AND `the days from` `the day I satisfied it` `to` `the day asked about` AT LEAST 0
        `the time satisfied` MEANS max 0 (`the days from` `the day the warning was provided` `to` `the day I satisfied it`)
        `the events` MEANS
            IF `satisfied by the day asked about`
            THEN LIST (EVENT `the complainant` `satisfy the Commissioner's requirement` `the time satisfied`)
            ELSE LIST (WAITUNTIL (`the days from` `the day the warning was provided` `to` `the day asked about`))
        `satisfied in the 14 days` MEANS
            CONSIDER EVALTRACE `s 25(7) -- satisfy the requirement within 14 days of the warning` 0 `the events`
            WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `ss 25(1), (1C), (1CA), 27 -- assessment and notice of it`

-- s 25(1): "The Commissioner must assess a complaint within 45 days after receiving it." (1C): the Commissioner may
-- extend the period "for an additional period not exceeding 45 days" (after an unsuccessful attempt at early resolution
-- under s 25A, or if necessary for assessment). (1CA): if there is a delay in obtaining information, "for such time as
-- is necessary". (1D): the complainant must be notified of an extension. An extension under (1C) beyond 45 days is
-- capped at 45 (fork F4).
GIVEN `the day the Commissioner received it` IS A DATE
      `days of extension under s 25(1C)` IS A NUMBER
      `days of extension under s 25(1CA)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 25(1) -- the last day for assessment` `the day the Commissioner received it` `days of extension under s 25(1C)` `days of extension under s 25(1CA)` MEANS
    `the day` (45 PLUS min 45 (max 0 `days of extension under s 25(1C)`) PLUS max 0 `days of extension under s 25(1CA)`) `days after` `the day the Commissioner received it`

-- s 27: "Within 14 days after making a determination under section 25 (1), the Commissioner must provide written notice
-- of the determination -- (a) to the complainant".
GIVEN `the day of the determination` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 27 -- the last day for notice of the assessment` `the day of the determination` MEANS `the day` 14 `days after` `the day of the determination`

§§ `s 30 -- withdrawal`

-- s 30(1): "A complainant may withdraw a complaint at any time by notifying the Commissioner in writing". (2): the
-- Commissioner must "(a) if the health service provider has been notified of the receipt of the complaint, notify that
-- provider of the withdrawal within 14 days; and (b) take no further action in relation to the complaint other than an
-- investigation under Part 6." The 14 days are counted from the written notice of withdrawal (fork F5). If the provider
-- was never notified, the duty does not arise: NOTHING-kind: no such duty, so no date.
GIVEN `the provider was notified of the complaint` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I gave written notice of withdrawal` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 30(2)(a) -- the last day to tell the provider` `the provider was notified of the complaint` `the day I gave written notice of withdrawal` MEANS
    IF `the provider was notified of the complaint`
    THEN JUST (`the day` 14 `days after` `the day I gave written notice of withdrawal`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `ss 25(4), 32A, 33, 37, 39 -- conciliation`

-- s 25(1A)(b)(i): the Commissioner may refer the complaint to a conciliator "if ... of the opinion that it is
-- appropriate". s 25(4): "The Commissioner must not refer a complaint to a conciliator if -- (a) the complaint appears
-- to the Commissioner to indicate -- (i) the existence of a significant issue of public safety or public interest; or
-- (ii) a significant question as to the practice of a health service provider; or (b) section 64 would prevent the
-- Commissioner from disclosing to the health service provider information that would enable the health service user to
-- be identified." A flat "must not" and an "if": JUST FALSE for each. (b) turns on the health service user's (the
-- patient's) identity only: s 64 protecting a complainant who is not the patient does not bar conciliation.
GIVEN `the Commissioner thinks conciliation appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it indicates a significant issue of public safety or public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it indicates a significant question about the provider's practice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the patient's identity must be kept from the provider under s 64` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25(1A), (4) -- my complaint can go to conciliation` `the Commissioner thinks conciliation appropriate` `it indicates a significant issue of public safety or public interest` `it indicates a significant question about the provider's practice` `the patient's identity must be kept from the provider under s 64` MEANS
    IF     `it indicates a significant issue of public safety or public interest`
        OR `it indicates a significant question about the provider's practice`
        OR `the patient's identity must be kept from the provider under s 64`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the Commissioner thinks conciliation appropriate`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 32A: "Where the Commissioner has referred a complaint for conciliation, the complainant and the health service
-- provider must attend an initial meeting, but any subsequent participation in the conciliation by the parties is
-- voluntary and either party may withdraw from the conciliation process at any time." JUST TRUE for the initial
-- meeting; JUST FALSE for later ones ("voluntary") and where there is no referral (a "where" that fails). The initial
-- meeting is a duty even though "either party may withdraw ... at any time" (fork F6).
GIVEN `the complaint was referred for conciliation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the initial meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 32A -- I must attend` `the complaint was referred for conciliation` `it is the initial meeting` MEANS
    IF `the complaint was referred for conciliation` AND `it is the initial meeting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 33: "A party in a conciliation process may not be represented by another person except where -- (a) the
-- Commissioner is satisfied that such representation is likely to assist substantially in resolving the complaint; and
-- (b) not less than 48 hours before requesting the Commissioner to allow such representation, that party has notified
-- the other party, in writing, that he or she will be making that request." A flat negative with an exception: JUST
-- FALSE when the exception is not met, JUST TRUE when it is (fork F7). The 48 hours are counted from the day and hour
-- of the written notice to the day and hour of the request; exactly 48 is enough.
GIVEN `the Commissioner is satisfied it would assist substantially` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I notified the other party in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of my notice` IS A DATE
      `the hour of my notice` IS A NUMBER
      `the day of my request` IS A DATE
      `the hour of my request` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33 -- I may be represented at conciliation` `the Commissioner is satisfied it would assist substantially` `I notified the other party in writing` `the day of my notice` `the hour of my notice` `the day of my request` `the hour of my request` MEANS
    IF     `the Commissioner is satisfied it would assist substantially`
       AND `I notified the other party in writing`
       AND `the hours between` AT LEAST 48
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `the hours between` MEANS
            (`the days from` `the day of my notice` `to` `the day of my request` TIMES 24) PLUS (`the hour of my request` MINUS `the hour of my notice`)

-- s 37(1): "Anything said or admitted during conciliation -- (a) is not admissible as evidence in a proceeding before a
-- court or tribunal; and (b) cannot be used by the Commissioner as a ground for investigation or inquiry." A flat
-- negative: JUST FALSE. For something said outside conciliation the section is silent: NOTHING-kind: the text is
-- silent.
GIVEN `it was said or admitted during conciliation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 37(1) -- it is admissible in court` `it was said or admitted during conciliation` MEANS
    IF `it was said or admitted during conciliation`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 39: "(1) Any agreement reached between a complainant and a health service provider in the course of the
-- conciliation process may be put in a form that is binding on them. (2) An agreement is not binding unless it is --
-- (a) in writing; and (b) entered into within 14 days after the verbal agreement is reached in the course of the
-- conciliation. (3) Subsection (1) does not affect the effectiveness of any agreement reached outside the conciliation
-- process."
--
-- The regulative rule: from the day the verbal agreement is reached (time 0) the parties must put it in writing within
-- 14 days, lest it is not binding.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
`s 39(2) -- put the agreement in writing within 14 days` MEANS
    PARTY `the parties to the conciliation`
    MUST `put the agreement in writing`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the parties to the conciliation` BECAUSE "an agreement reached in conciliation is not binding unless it is in writing and entered into within 14 days after the verbal agreement (s 39(2))"

-- "not binding unless": JUST FALSE when it is not in writing within the 14 days. Once the "unless" is met, JUST TRUE if
-- the parties put it in a form binding on them (s 39(1)); otherwise NOTHING-kind: points outside the sources (the
-- general law of contract) (fork F8). An agreement reached outside conciliation: NOTHING-kind: points outside the
-- sources (s 39(3)).
GIVEN `it was reached in the course of conciliation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the verbal agreement` IS A DATE
      `the day the written agreement was entered into` IS A DATE
      `we put it in a form binding on us` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 39 -- our conciliation agreement is binding` `it was reached in the course of conciliation` `it is in writing` `the day of the verbal agreement` `the day the written agreement was entered into` `we put it in a form binding on us` MEANS
    IF (NOT `it was reached in the course of conciliation`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF (NOT `in writing in time`)
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF `we put it in a form binding on us`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `the time written` MEANS max 0 (`the days from` `the day of the verbal agreement` `to` `the day the written agreement was entered into`)
        `in writing in time` MEANS
            IF `it is in writing`
            THEN CONSIDER EVALTRACE `s 39(2) -- put the agreement in writing within 14 days` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the parties to the conciliation` `put the agreement in writing` `the time written`))
                 WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
                 OTHERWISE FALSE
            ELSE FALSE

§§ `ss 40(1), 55(2) -- the investigation report`

-- s 40(1): the Commissioner may investigate "(a) any matter specified in a written direction given by the Health
-- Minister; (b) a complaint that the Commissioner has determined to investigate under section 25(1A)(b)(ii); (c) an
-- issue or question arising from a complaint" of significant public safety or interest or practice; "(d) on his or her
-- own motion, any other matter ...; (e) ... any matter relating to a possible breach of a code of conduct by a health
-- care worker". s 55(2): "A copy of each report is to be provided to -- ... (f) if the investigation is one referred to
-- in section 40 (1) (b) or (c), the complainant". An "if": JUST FALSE for the other kinds (finding 5).
DECLARE `Kind of investigation` IS ONE OF
    `an investigation of my complaint`
    `an investigation of an issue or question arising from my complaint`
    `an investigation of a possible breach of a code of conduct by a health care worker`
    `an investigation directed by the Health Minister`
    `an investigation of another matter on the Commissioner's own motion`

GIVEN `the investigation` IS A `Kind of investigation`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 55(2)(f) -- I am to be given a copy of the report` `the investigation` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the investigation`
    WHEN `an investigation of my complaint` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an investigation of an issue or question arising from my complaint` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 56AAD(2)(a) -- the statement of decision on a prohibition order`

-- s 56AAD(1): if the Commissioner makes a prohibition order, a written statement of decision goes to the health care
-- worker. (2): "the Commissioner -- (a) in the case of a prohibition order made as the result of a complaint, must
-- provide a copy of the statement of decision ... to the complainant", subject to the removal of confidential
-- information (3), (4). "In the case of" counts as "where": JUST FALSE when the order was not made as the result of my
-- complaint, or no order was made. An interim prohibition order (s 56AAB) has its statement of decision given only to
-- the worker (s 56AAB(6)): NOTHING-kind: the text is silent on the complainant.
DECLARE `Order made` IS ONE OF
    `a prohibition order`
    `an interim prohibition order`
    `no order`

GIVEN `the order` IS A `Order made`
      `it was made as the result of my complaint` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 56AAD(2)(a) -- I am to be given the statement of decision` `the order` `it was made as the result of my complaint` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the order`
    WHEN `a prohibition order` THEN
        IF `it was made as the result of my complaint` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHEN `an interim prohibition order` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 56 -- the provider's answer to a notice of recommended action`

-- s 56(1): after investigating, if the complaint is justified but appears incapable of being resolved, the Commissioner
-- may give the provider a notice of recommended action and advise the complainant. (3): "A health service provider to
-- whom a notice is provided must, within 45 days after receiving the notice or such longer period as the Commissioner
-- allows under subsection (4), advise the Commissioner, in writing, of what action he, she or it has taken in order to
-- remedy the grievances referred to in the notice. Penalty: Fine not exceeding 50 penalty units." (4): "If the
-- Commissioner receives before the end of the period of 45 days ... a written request by a health service provider to
-- extend that period, the Commissioner may extend that period by not more than 15 days." An extension asked for late,
-- or longer than 15 days, counts only up to what (4) allows (fork F9).
GIVEN `the provider asked in writing before the 45 days ended` IS A BOOLEAN
      `days of extension the Commissioner allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 56(3), (4) -- the days the provider has` `the provider asked in writing before the 45 days ended` `days of extension the Commissioner allowed` MEANS
    IF `the provider asked in writing before the 45 days ended`
    THEN 45 PLUS min 15 (max 0 `days of extension the Commissioner allowed`)
    ELSE 45

GIVEN `the day the provider received the notice` IS A DATE
      `the provider asked in writing before the 45 days ended` IS A BOOLEAN
      `days of extension the Commissioner allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 56(3) -- the provider's last day` `the day the provider received the notice` `the provider asked in writing before the 45 days ended` `days of extension the Commissioner allowed` MEANS
    `the day` (`s 56(3), (4) -- the days the provider has` `the provider asked in writing before the 45 days ended` `days of extension the Commissioner allowed`) `days after` `the day the provider received the notice`

-- The regulative rule: from the day the provider receives the notice (time 0).
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
`s 56(3) -- advise the Commissioner within the period` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the health service provider`
    MUST `advise the Commissioner of the action taken`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the health service provider` BECAUSE "the provider did not advise the Commissioner in writing of the action taken within 45 days after receiving the notice (or the extended period): an offence, fine not exceeding 50 penalty units (s 56(3))"

DECLARE `The provider's answer` IS ONE OF
    `the provider answered in time`
    `the provider did not answer in time, an offence with a fine of up to 50 penalty units`
    `the provider's time has not yet run out`

GIVEN `the day the provider received the notice` IS A DATE
      `the provider asked in writing before the 45 days ended` IS A BOOLEAN
      `days of extension the Commissioner allowed` IS A NUMBER
      `the provider has advised the Commissioner in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the provider advised` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `The provider's answer`
`s 56(3) -- the provider's answer` `the day the provider received the notice` `the provider asked in writing before the 45 days ended` `days of extension the Commissioner allowed` `the provider has advised the Commissioner in writing` `the day the provider advised` `the day asked about` MEANS
    IF `answered in time`
    THEN `the provider answered in time`
    ELSE IF `the time asked about` GREATER THAN `the days allowed`
         THEN `the provider did not answer in time, an offence with a fine of up to 50 penalty units`
         ELSE `the provider's time has not yet run out`
    WHERE
        `the days allowed` MEANS `s 56(3), (4) -- the days the provider has` `the provider asked in writing before the 45 days ended` `days of extension the Commissioner allowed`
        `the time asked about` MEANS `the days from` `the day the provider received the notice` `to` `the day asked about`
        `the time advised` MEANS max 0 (`the days from` `the day the provider received the notice` `to` `the day the provider advised`)
        `advised by the day asked about` MEANS
            `the provider has advised the Commissioner in writing`
            AND `the time advised` AT MOST `the time asked about`
        `answered in time` MEANS
            IF `advised by the day asked about`
            THEN CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`s 56(3) -- advise the Commissioner within the period` `the days allowed`) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the health service provider` `advise the Commissioner of the action taken` `the time advised`))
                 WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
                 OTHERWISE FALSE
            ELSE FALSE

§§ `s 64 -- my identity`

-- s 64(1): "Notwithstanding any other provision of this Act, the Commissioner must not disclose to a health service
-- provider information that would enable a health service user or a complainant to be identified if the Commissioner
-- believes, on reasonable grounds, that the disclosure would, directly or indirectly -- (a) put at risk the health or
-- safety of any person; or (b) occasion the receipt by a person of a health service of a lower standard ...; or (c)
-- prejudice the assessment of a complaint or an investigation". JUST TRUE (it must be withheld) when the Commissioner
-- holds the belief; otherwise NOTHING-kind: the text is silent (the Act does not say the identity must be disclosed;
-- s 64(2) requires disclosure only of information once withheld under (1)).
GIVEN `the Commissioner believes disclosure would risk health or safety, a lower standard of service, or the assessment or investigation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 64(1) -- my identity must be kept from the provider` `the Commissioner believes disclosure would risk health or safety, a lower standard of service, or the assessment or investigation` MEANS
    IF `the Commissioner believes disclosure would risk health or safety, a lower standard of service, or the assessment or investigation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `ss 67, 68, 71 -- intimidation and reprisals`

DECLARE `Offence answer` IS ONE OF
    `an offence, with a fine of up to 100 penalty units`
    `this section gives the person a defence on these facts`
    `not an offence under this section on these facts`

-- s 67(1): "Without reasonable excuse, a person must not persuade or attempt to persuade by threat or intimidation
-- another person -- (a) to refrain from making to the Commissioner or any other person a complaint; or (b) to withdraw a
-- complaint; or (c) to fail to co-operate with the Commissioner ...; or (d) to fail to provide information or a
-- document ...; or (e) to provide information or a document that is false or misleading ... Penalty: Fine not exceeding
-- 100 penalty units." (2): "It is a defence ... that -- (a) the defendant had another ground for engaging in the conduct
-- alleged; and (b) that ground is a reasonable one."
GIVEN `I was threatened or intimidated to stop me complaining, make me withdraw, or stop me co-operating or giving information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person had another, reasonable ground for the conduct` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Offence answer`
`s 67 -- intimidation` `I was threatened or intimidated to stop me complaining, make me withdraw, or stop me co-operating or giving information` `the person had a reasonable excuse` `the person had another, reasonable ground for the conduct` MEANS
    IF (NOT `I was threatened or intimidated to stop me complaining, make me withdraw, or stop me co-operating or giving information`) OR `the person had a reasonable excuse`
    THEN `not an offence under this section on these facts`
    ELSE IF `the person had another, reasonable ground for the conduct`
         THEN `this section gives the person a defence on these facts`
         ELSE `an offence, with a fine of up to 100 penalty units`

-- s 68(1): "A person must not take, attempt to take or conspire to take a reprisal against another person because, or
-- in the belief that, any person -- (a) has made or may make a complaint; or (b) has co-operated ... with the
-- Commissioner ...; or (c) has provided ... documents or information ... Penalty: Fine not exceeding 100 penalty units."
-- (2): examples of a reprisal: failing to employ a person, dismissing a person from employment, penalising or
-- discriminating against a person in employment. (3): it is enough that the ground is "a significant factor". (5): it
-- is a defence for the defendant to prove that "(a) the defendant had another ground for engaging in that conduct; and
-- (b) that ground is a reasonable one; and (c) the defendant had taken a significant step towards engaging in that
-- conduct before acting on the ground specified in subsection (1)." When the defence is not proved: JUST FALSE for the
-- defence, worded "this section gives ... a defence on these facts" (rulings of 2026-11-05 (b)).
GIVEN `a reprisal was taken, attempted or conspired against me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my complaint or co-operation was a significant factor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person had another, reasonable ground` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person took a significant step towards it beforehand` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Offence answer`
`s 68 -- reprisal` `a reprisal was taken, attempted or conspired against me` `my complaint or co-operation was a significant factor` `the person had another, reasonable ground` `the person took a significant step towards it beforehand` MEANS
    IF (NOT `a reprisal was taken, attempted or conspired against me`) OR (NOT `my complaint or co-operation was a significant factor`)
    THEN `not an offence under this section on these facts`
    ELSE IF `the person had another, reasonable ground` AND `the person took a significant step towards it beforehand`
         THEN `this section gives the person a defence on these facts`
         ELSE `an offence, with a fine of up to 100 penalty units`

-- s 71: "Proceedings for an offence against this Act are to start -- (a) within 6 months after the commission of the
-- offence; or (b) within 6 months after the offence comes to the knowledge of the Commissioner." Either limb will do,
-- so the later of the two last days governs (finding 7). "within 6 months after" a day ends on the corresponding day 6
-- months later (fork F1).
GIVEN `the day of the offence` IS A DATE
      `the day it came to the Commissioner's knowledge` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 71 -- the last day to start a prosecution` `the day of the offence` `the day it came to the Commissioner's knowledge` MEANS
    `the later of` (`the corresponding day` 6 `months after` `the day of the offence`) `and` (`the corresponding day` 6 `months after` `the day it came to the Commissioner's knowledge`)

§§ `s 73 -- protection from civil actions`

-- s 73: "A person is not liable in respect of loss, damage or injury of any kind suffered by another person as a result
-- of any of the following done in good faith: (a) the making of a complaint; ... (b) the making of a statement, the
-- provision of any information ... or ... any document for the purposes of this Act to the Commissioner, a conciliator
-- or another person authorized to receive" it. A flat "is not liable": the protection is JUST TRUE in good faith. Not in
-- good faith, s 73 gives nothing and the general law decides: NOTHING-kind: points outside the sources.
GIVEN `I acted in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73 -- I am protected from liability for complaining` `I acted in good faith` MEANS
    IF `I acted in good faith`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
